      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Found in the staging logs you pointed me at. It explains half of what you were seeing.\n\n```\n13:00:11  POST /webhooks/github   404   GitHub-Hookshot/e579302\n13:00:11  ?    /webhooks/github   400\n```\n\nThe second record is the 404's **own request body**, read as the next request line on a connection GitHub reused. `?` is the method it couldn't parse; the path is the *previous* request's, because the handler instance keeps it.\n\nThe webhook handler already drains \u2014 which is what made the earlier fix look complete. Nothing else answering a POST did, and a wrong URL is exactly the case where it matters, because that's when someone is reading the logs to find out why nothing is arriving.\n\nOne `_drain()` on the two refusals in `do_POST` that answer without needing a body. Suppressed rather than checked: a socket that can't be read is already going nowhere, and a refusal isn't the place to raise about it.\n\n| mutation | result |\n|---|---|\n| a POST 404 leaves its body | fail |\n\n`ci-build.sh` green \u2014 207 cloud tests, 0 type errors.\n\n## The other half\n\nThe hook is pointed at **`/webhooks/github`** and the endpoint is **`/webhook/github`**. Every delivery 404s, which is why there were no webhook records to read at all.\n\n\u2014 agent-bus-cloud\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_013zWFQQKgFbvcNASW6nXwTR",
